    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="1094" n="1078" sameAs="frus:frus1950v04/pg1078"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.21/1–1050: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Kirk</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-01-10">January 10,
                        1950</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. <hi rendition="#italic">Pravda</hi> January 9, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Izvestiya</hi> January 10 print New York Tass<anchor n="1" xml:id="d588-f1"
                    /> item headed “sharp deterioration economic position US” on report economic
                    advisers. Washington Tass item on President’s economic message Congress,<anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d588-f2"/> total one column. Treatment same line as given
                    State of Union message<anchor n="3" xml:id="d588-f3"/> emphasizes drop
                    production, growth unemployment and strikes, deficit federal budget, housing
                    shortage, inadequacy Social Security, natural resources, education, health
                    programs, drop wages and farm income, increase military expenses, decline
                    exports.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kirk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d588-f1" n="1" xml:id="d588-f1-content">
                <p>Telegraph Agency of the Soviet Union, the official communications organization of
                    the Soviet Government.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d588-f2" n="2" xml:id="d588-f2-content">
                <p>The President’s annual economic report was given to the Congress on January 6.
                    For the text of the message, see <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the
                        Presidents of the United States: Harry S. Truman, 1950</hi> (Washington,
                    Government Printing Office, 1965), pp. 18–31. The message and complete report
                    were printed as <hi rendition="#italic">The Economic Report of the President
                        Transmitted to the Congress, January 6, 1950</hi> (Washington, Government
                    Printing Office, 1950).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d588-f3" n="3" xml:id="d588-f3-content">
                <p>This address was delivered in person before a joint session of the Congress on
                    January 4. For the text, see <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the
                        Presidents of the United States: Harry S. Truman, 1950</hi>, pp. 2–11.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
